    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="19" relname="span">The Medicare website was a great example of applying the senior-friendly guidelines for web design that the NIA/NLM has recommended.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="20" relname="span">My first thought when I visited the site was whether or not I had accidentally adjusted my screen resolution to a larger font size.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="elaboration">In other words the font size was clearly legible, which is an important factor when attempting to accommodate for those individuals with poor or failing eyesight.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="19" relname="evidence">Links to various topics had on mouse click features which is another important factor for those with physical impairment.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="18" relname="evidence">The wording and literacy content is also easily read and easily understood;</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="17" relname="evidence">the site also converts to espanol for Spanish speaking individuals.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="21" relname="span">I couldnt find a sitemap which would be helpful to outline all the various aspects and avenues of the site;</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="7" relname="elaboration">a great way for individuals with cognitive issues to clearly view links to specific areas at a broad outlook.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="15" relname="evidence">The site is void of busy and distractible features that one might come to expect and possibly enjoy in todays websites.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="14" relname="evidence">The site purposefully utilizes usability factors that would accommodate individuals with specific disadvantages;</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="13" relname="summary">a great example of a senior friendly-site.</segment>
        <group id="12" type="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="14" relname="span"/>
